  "body": "### Summary\n\nCapture on the Mac, with the LOT-001 (#38) kit (`tooling/fixtures/`), the page state: Moderator alert: submit success (text, refresh, \"avec succès\"?)\n\n### Scope\n\nState to capture: Moderator alert: submit success (text, refresh, \"avec succès\"?)\n\nNote: until captured, an alert write cannot be classified `success`\n\nRules: anonymize every free-text field; never hand-build the state in the cloud (LESSONS 36); add a legacy oracle when a parser consumes it (LOT-002 (#39)..005 tooling); one PR per batch of captures; the PR removes the row from the Capture backlog.\n\n### Wanted by\n\nLOT-037 (#64), LOT-050 (#76)\n\n### Depends on\n\n—\n\n### Owner / session\n\n— (ready; `host: mac`)\n\n### Source\n\n`docs/LOTS.md` \"Capture backlog (Mac)\", copied from the frozen old issue [francoisgn/ios-app_SwiftHFR#98](https://github.com/francoisgn/ios-app_SwiftHFR/issues/98).\n",
